# Failing-first relaunch replay in tests/fm-spawn-relaunch-live-clone.test.sh: a ship recorded in an older same-origin clone, its tmux pane standing in its claimed old-pool slot, relaunches onto a leased live-pool slot at the same branch head (pane told to cd there, claims moved, record naming the live clone); on the base it relaunches in the old clone's worktree, and at 9317a7cd the tmux pane is refused. A relaunch refusing after the move rolls it back, a different live branch is never overwritten, and an ssh and an https URL of one repository read as one origin; each fails at 9317a7cd. A rollback after the pane moved sends it back before the slot is returned, and a copy not on its branch is refused; both fail at b8d960bd. Submodules land on the recorded commits with the slot clean, and an unpushed submodule commit refuses and rolls back; both fail at fb84a68c. A foreign-clone slot is skipped and returned, a lone foreign lease is returned on refusal, and a slot another task claims is never taken or returned; each fails at 3b098dcf. A claimed slot handed out first is skipped and the move takes the free slot after it; fails at 8e5d476e. The move refuses while the shared Treehouse project lock is held, when a claimed slot has nothing running in it, and when the live pool cannot be read, before leasing anything; each fails at 31478b53. From 6ebb0f81 on, the move never asks Treehouse's allocator for a slot (it takes a free live-clone slot by name). From 32a685f3 on, the move rewrites the task's record to name the live slot before any endpoint is touched, so a later refusal leaves the task consistent on the live clone; a rollback inside the move leaves the slot exactly clean even when the branch added a submodule, and an edit in an ignored submodule counts as uncommitted work; each fails at 32a685f3. A free slot whose ignored submodule holds an edit is never taken, and a relaunch after a pane that did not follow finishes the move; both fail at ea0eded5. A strictly dirty lowest slot is passed over for a clean one, and a retry never finishes a move over work made in the old copy since; both fail at c30bb1da. A retry never finishes a move over a commit made in the old copy since (the old copy counts as carried only when clean and its HEAD is in the live slot's history); fails at 5bb5bab5.
pr: 171
